  "term": "solvent",
  "definition": "In biological sample preparation, a solvent is a liquid used in stepwise exchange procedures, such as graded ethanol series, to dehydrate or rehydrate tissues. These solvent changes help prepare specimens for staining, clearing, and microscope imaging.",
